; Live tests drive a real GTK display, so they run only under xvfb and only when
; explicitly asked for:
;   BONSAI_GTK_LIVE_TESTS=1 xvfb-run -a dune build @test/live/runtest
;
; The eleven rules whose executable presents a toplevel carry `(locks x-display)`.
; One `xvfb-run` gives every executable below the same X display, and a window
; mapping on a display takes the input focus off whichever window held it -- so a
; neighbour starting up mid-test is indistinguishable, to
; `live_controllers_focus.ml`, from the focus controller losing focus on its own:
; an intermittent
; golden diff that reads as a regression in the controller. Measured
; unserialised: 1 run in 10 fails, 3 in 7 on a loaded machine, 4 in 7 on a very
; loaded one. Serialised: 0 focus failures in 6 loaded runs, 0 in 15 with the
; older `-j 1`.
;
; `(locks x-display)` rather than `-j 1` on one call site (final review, live
; lens), for two reasons. It binds the constraint to the *rules*, so `dune test`,
; `dune build @test/live/runtest` with no flags, an editor's run-tests action and
; anything else that reaches these rules all inherit it -- `-j 1` protected one
; line in one script and nothing else. And it serialises only these rule actions:
; measured on a cold tree, `-j 1` costs 26 s (59 s against 33 s) because it also
; serialises compiling and linking every executable here (twelve at the time of
; the measurement), where the lock costs 1 s.
; Warm -- which is what ci.sh always is -- the two are indistinguishable at ~31 s.
;
; `live_events` and `live_keyvals` deliberately have no lock: neither calls
; `GMain.init` and both run to completion with DISPLAY unset. They live here
; because `test/` links only `bonsai_gtk.vtree` and they need ocgtk, not because
; they touch X. `live_controllers_click` initialises GTK but presents no
; toplevel -- its two blocks mount bare labels -- so it takes no lock either.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{env:BONSAI_GTK_LIVE_TESTS=0} 1))
 (deps live_patcher.exe)
 (locks x-display)
 (action
  (progn
   (with-stdout-to
    output_patcher.txt
    (run %{exe:live_patcher.exe}))
   (diff expected_patcher.txt output_patcher.txt))))

